  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "In October 2026, Mollica announced that Joe Locke would reprise his MCU role of Billy Maximoff from Agatha All Along in VisionQuest.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383842888:76"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Locke is expected to return as Billy Maximoff, Wanda and Vision's sorcerer son and Tommy's younger twin, whose soul inhabited William Kaplan's body after his death in Agatha All Along.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383842888:15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "VisionQuest is an American television miniseries created by Terry Matalas for Disney+, based on Marvel Comics featuring the character Vision.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383842888:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The series stars Paul Bettany, James Spader, Ruaridh Mollica and Todd Stashwick among others, with music by Mick Giacchino.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1383842888:starring",
        "wiki:box:1383842888:music"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:37Z",
      "text": "From late March to early April, filming took place at a local pub in the Chiltern Hills, England, which served as the location for The Old Selkie pub.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1383842888:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "Principal photography began by March 14, 2025, at Pinewood Studios in London, under the working title Tin Man.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1383842888:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "The article places filming at Chiltern Hills, Scotland, Pinewood Studios, Hatfield House, White Waltham Airfield and 1 more location.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1383842888:0",
        "wiki:film:1383842888:1",
        "wiki:film:1383842888:2",
        "wiki:film:1383842888:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:00Z",
      "text": "16 of the people credited have a birthplace on record, and 8 of them were born in the United Kingdom.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q115781248:P19",
        "wd:Q115793922:P19",
        "wd:Q117500:P19",
        "wd:Q124325356:P19",
        "wd:Q242707:P19",
        "wd:Q296928:P19",
        "wd:Q3052376:P19",
        "wd:Q444292:P19",
        "wd:Q4885474:P19",
        "wd:Q5271532:P19",
        "wd:Q5357354:P19",
        "wd:Q63993432:P19",
        "wd:Q64853354:P19",
        "wd:Q705644:P19",
        "wd:Q717194:P19",
        "wd:Q7225794:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:08Z",
      "text": "Several were born further afield, including Ruaridh Mollica in Prato, Italy, Mary McDonnell in Wilkes-Barre, United States, and James Spader in Boston, United States.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q115781248:P19",
        "wd:Q117500:P19",
        "wd:Q296928:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:18Z",
      "text": "157,657 people read the article on 4 November 2026, about 14 times the usual number.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:VisionQuest:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:VisionQuest:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:24Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, Italian had the most readers at 6,743.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:VisionQuest:2026-11-04",
        "views:it:VisionQuest:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:30Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not the same as a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:it:VisionQuest:2026-11-04",
        "views:es:VisionQuest:2026-11-04",
        "views:fr:VisionQuest:2026-11-04",
